    "Decision": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "description": "A human (or automated) call that overrides the computed result for one target.\n\n``UPHOLD`` forces the target to the policy floor, ``REFUTE`` neutralises it, ``VACATED``\nwithdraws a previous stance and restores the computed value. How each is applied depends on\nthe family of the target — an observable is bounded, a claim is taken out of the count — but\nthat is the engine's dispatch, not a second axis of this model.\n\n``justification`` is required: an override whose reason is optional is an override that\ncannot be audited, which defeats the point of recording it as a fact at all.",
      "properties": {
        "key": {
          "minLength": 1,
          "title": "Key",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "seq": {
          "maxLength": 26,
          "minLength": 26,
          "title": "Seq",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "asserted_at": {
          "format": "date-time",
          "title": "Asserted At",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "occurred_at": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "format": "date-time",
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null,
          "title": "Occurred At"
        },
        "source": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/SourceRef"
        },
        "fragment_id": {
          "title": "Fragment Id",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "external_id": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null,
          "title": "External Id"
        },
        "evidence_keys": {
          "default": [],
          "items": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "title": "Evidence Keys",
          "type": "array"
        },
        "target_key": {
          "minLength": 1,
          "title": "Target Key",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "kind": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/DecisionKind"
        },
        "justification": {
          "minLength": 1,
          "title": "Justification",
          "type": "string"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "key",
        "seq",
        "asserted_at",
        "source",
        "fragment_id",
        "target_key",
        "kind",
        "justification"
      ],
      "title": "Decision",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "DecisionKind": {
      "description": "A named override of the computation.\n\nForcing a score has to be a declared act — never the side effect of an inflated weight.\n\nThe kind states the **intent**; the mechanism follows from the family of the target, which\nthe key already carries. An earlier design enumerated one value per ``(intent, family)``\npair — ``ALLOWLISTED``/``BLOCKLISTED``/``CONFIRMED``/``DISMISSED`` — and then needed a\nvalidator to forbid the half of that product which made no sense. An enum requiring a\nvalidator to reject half its combinations encodes one axis too many: the family is the\ntarget's business, not the decision's.\n\nThe domain vocabulary survives untouched on the façade (``allowlist``, ``blocklist``,\n``confirm``, ``dismiss``), where it belongs.",
      "enum": [
        "UPHOLD",
        "REFUTE",
        "VACATED"
      ],
      "title": "DecisionKind",
      "type": "string"
    },
    "Effect": {
      "description": "How a finding enters the investigation total. :class:`Status` says *whether*, this says *how*.\n\n``ADDITIVE`` is every finding v6 ever had: a term of the sum.\n\n``FLOOR`` is a **conclusion** — typically an AI analysis that read the other findings. It is\nnot a term: it raises the total just enough to reach the verdict it asserts, and adds nothing\nwhen that verdict is already reached. Conclusions therefore never compound, which is what\nmakes it safe to plug several analysers into the same investigation.\n\nThe floor a verdict maps to is ``basic-v1``'s band convention, like every other number here —\nsee :mod:`cyvest.evaluation.projection`.",
      "enum": [
        "ADDITIVE",
        "FLOOR"
      ],
      "title": "Effect",
      "type": "string"
    },
